nce fgfr  2b and 2c variants it can be used to  look at fusion junctions  you can also detect specifically target  sequences that are members of highly  complex gene families moreover it can be  used for point mutation detection  and also illustrations of that as well  this slide is from the first publication  with the rna scope assay and simply is  to  demonstrate the the fact that what we  detect with rna scope  as dots visual dots correspond to  individual molecules of rna  this is a simple cell culture experiment  where hela cells were tested  with an rna scope probe to her2 on the  left-hand side you can see  visual green dots and there are  approximately 14  dots per cell in a field of view in  comparison  another plate of helo cells had rna  extracted  and measured in solution with a standard  curve of in vitro transcribe message  in that way an average value of 17  copies of of her2 rna could be measured  on a per cell basis and so these two  numbers 17 copies per cell on average  from a lysate and 14 dots per cell  are very similar and this is to show  that  an individual molecule is being detected  when we see dots  in a fixed cell or fixed tissue  this assay was used by the lab of the  late ray tubbs at the cleveland clinic  as a means of differentiating or  resolving i should say  cases where her2 status was equivocal  based on either ihc or or dna fish  what uh the rate the lab of ray tubbs  did  was to measure her to transcript level  in breast cancer  and determine a molecular threshold that  corresponded to her2 positivity  in comparison to ihc this is a bit of a  busy  uh figure but the the primary point here  is that  using a molecular cutoff of her2  measured  by rna scope in the first place they can  show  a very good concordance between cases  where  ihc is equivocal but fish is negative  for her2 amplification  and rna scope signal is also negative in  the middle  you're seeing cases where ihc again is  equivocal  but it's fish positive for amplification  of the her2 locus  and likewise her2 transcript levels are  also amplified above that molecular  threshold  the important uh data set was in cases  where both ihc  and fish were equivocal and could not uh  firmly establish the  the role of her2 in in breast cancer  in this case what's shown is the same  molecular cutoff can be used to  define a patient as being positive above  the threshold or negative  below that threshold so this is just a  point about the  ability to use molecular quantification  of a  transcript in this case her2 to define  a patient as being positive or negative  and potentially responsive to  a targeted therapeutic this in the next  few slides will show examples where rna  scope was determined to be more  sensitive and specific than  other methods for measuring uh specific  biomarkers that were  a predictive or appear to be predictive  of patient response to  an oncology targeted therapeutic the  example shown here is for  merrimack pharmaceuticals mm-121 anti or  b3 therapeutic  where they determined that it was  actually the ligand growth factor  hergulin  or nrg1 which was a predictive or at  least correlated with response to  their therapeutic m120 mn121  now the fact that nrg1 is a growth  factor and secreted  excreted protein made it very difficult  to detect it by ihc  in intact tissue biopsies and the fact  that they were getting  very small needle biopsies from the  patient  did not provide them with sufficient  material material to get a reliable  qpcr readout moreover the spatial  resolution  of the rna scope assay enabled them to  verify  the presence of heregolan expression in  the tumor itself as opposed to in  adjacent stromal cells and these factors  contributed to its utility  as a potential biomarker assay  shown here is retrospective data from  phase one clinical trials in breast  cancer ovarian cancer and lung cancer  where  they observe that high levels of  irregulin as measured by  the rna scope assay appeared to identify  a sub-population of patients which were  responsive and showed longer  progression-free survival  in comparison to patients with low  heregulan expression  it was based on these results that they  used this assay as the basis for patient  selection  in in a phase ii clinical trial  rna scope also proved to be a very  effective biomarker assay for  bears fgfr one two and three small  molecule tyrosine kinase inhibitor  in this case it showed superior  performance compared to  ihc and nanostring and the starting  point for this was the fact that  historically  gene amplification and genomic  alterations of fgfr  genes has been used as a way to identify  patients for um  for small molecule tyrosine kinase  inhibitors however uh published reports  show that  there actually was not a very good  correlation between uh tki sensitivity  uh and gene amplification and in fact  expression was a better predictor and  based on these results they used the rna  scope assay for  as a basis for enrollment in their phase  one clinical trial  as well as their phase two clinical  trials in both cases both clinical  trials  there was a very uh high rate of  response to  their tyrosine kinase inhibitor in  patients that were selected with the rna  scope assay  and this isn't just in one illustration  here a case where there was no genomic  alteration  in this patient's biopsy uh however  there was  a significant increase in fgfr rna  expression  and this patient did in fact respond  very well to  treatment this was observed in a very  large percentage of the patients that  were enrolled in this trial  the idea one checkpoint target is  another  good illustration of where methods like  rna scope  can be more effective than more  well-established  approaches like ihc in oncology  ihc is probably the default method that  people think about when they think about  a biomarker assay however  oftentimes it will be the case that  newer assays like rna scope as well as  exosome diag